## Resubmission

This is a resubmission of version 0.1.0. In addition to carrying over the
previous round's fixes (software names in single quotes in Title and
Description; `\value` tags added to all exported functions), this version
also:

* Added `\examples` to the exported `print.*` methods that were still
  missing them, for consistency with the package's other exported functions.
* Removed unconditional Suggests dependencies from examples. Examples for
  `lingam_direct_bootstrap()` and its helper functions now use
  `reg_method = "ols"` (base R only), and examples that genuinely need a
  Suggests package (`DiagrammeR`, `ggplot2`) are now guarded with
  `requireNamespace()`.
* Fixed the "no visible binding for global variable 'lx' / 'ly'" NOTE from
  the previous round (missing `utils::globalVariables()` entries for
  `ggplot2::aes()` columns).
* Fixed several correctness issues found during an internal review (a
  condition in the kernel-based independence measure that silently ignored
  soft prior knowledge, an unsupported `reg_method = "ridge"` combination in
  the bootstrap total-effect step, and a data-scale dependence in the
  default adaptive-LASSO regularization path) and expanded the test suite
  accordingly.

